WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:03.010
- You can only stay on
the sidelines for so long.

00:00:03.010 --> 00:00:06.110
These are unprecedented times,

00:00:06.110 --> 00:00:08.300
and it seems like every day,

00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:11.260
the rule of law is being
eroded little by little.

00:00:11.260 --> 00:00:13.350
And frankly I'm sick of it.

00:00:13.350 --> 00:00:16.100
So I'm going to do something about it.

00:00:16.100 --> 00:00:18.560
I'm suing the White House, the CIA,

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:21.300
the Department of Justice
and a whole bunch of others.

00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:22.360
This is not a joke.

00:00:22.360 --> 00:00:24.060
This is actually happening.

00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:25.480
Let me give you some background.

00:00:25.480 --> 00:00:27.540
You might recall that back in January,

00:00:27.540 --> 00:00:29.270
President Trump was impeached

00:00:29.270 --> 00:00:31.440
and he was facing a trial in the Senate.

00:00:31.440 --> 00:00:33.829
- Article one is adopted.

00:00:33.829 --> 00:00:34.895
(gavel thumping)

00:00:34.895 --> 00:00:36.210
(senators clapping)

00:00:36.210 --> 00:00:37.890
- And one of the people
that seem to have a lot

00:00:37.890 --> 00:00:40.280
to say about the particular
charges that were levied

00:00:40.280 --> 00:00:41.290
against the President,

00:00:41.290 --> 00:00:44.170
was former National Security
Advisor John Bolton.

00:00:44.170 --> 00:00:46.410
And in what can only be described

00:00:46.410 --> 00:00:48.810
as an act of pure cowardice,

00:00:48.810 --> 00:00:51.680
John Bolton refused to
testify before the Senate.

00:00:51.680 --> 00:00:56.010
And instead decided to write
a book with his observations

00:00:56.010 --> 00:00:58.930
and presumably the things that
he would have testified to

00:00:58.930 --> 00:01:01.020
at the Senate trial of the President.

00:01:01.020 --> 00:01:03.700
- I didn't think the Democrats had the wit

00:01:03.700 --> 00:01:06.750
or the political
understanding or the reach.

00:01:06.750 --> 00:01:08.810
- Now that's problematic for a whole host

00:01:08.810 --> 00:01:11.400
of legal and moral reasons.

00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:12.960
But one of the legal issues is that,

00:01:12.960 --> 00:01:15.190
as a former National Security Advisor,

00:01:15.190 --> 00:01:18.050
in order to publish a book,
Bolton had to go through

00:01:18.050 --> 00:01:20.770
an onerous pre-publication review process.

00:01:20.770 --> 00:01:23.550
During the course of that
review process, the government

00:01:23.550 --> 00:01:25.910
would likely take out a
whole bunch of information

00:01:25.910 --> 00:01:28.490
that it doesn't want to be published.

00:01:28.490 --> 00:01:30.380
And I didn't trust the government

00:01:30.380 --> 00:01:33.670
to do that pre-publication
review and censoring

00:01:33.670 --> 00:01:35.690
of John Bolton's book in good faith.

00:01:35.690 --> 00:01:38.660
Under normal circumstances, but
doubly so when we're talking

00:01:38.660 --> 00:01:41.720
about things that strike at
the heart of our democracy

00:01:41.720 --> 00:01:44.070
and the President's impeachment trial.

00:01:44.070 --> 00:01:47.570
So back in February, I
filed some FOIA requests

00:01:47.570 --> 00:01:49.280
against the National Security Council,

00:01:49.280 --> 00:01:50.740
the CIA, the Department of Defense,

00:01:50.740 --> 00:01:52.880
the Department of Justice,
the Department of State,

00:01:52.880 --> 00:01:56.130
basically anyone that would
have possibly gotten a copy

00:01:56.130 --> 00:01:59.420
of John Bolton's book and had
something to say about it.

00:01:59.420 --> 00:02:01.160
Now, normally under this review process,

00:02:01.160 --> 00:02:03.930
the government can simply say
that this portion of the book,

00:02:03.930 --> 00:02:06.370
is classified and therefore
it cannot be published

00:02:06.370 --> 00:02:07.840
and there's some back and forth.

00:02:07.840 --> 00:02:10.240
But there's nothing that
forces the government

00:02:10.240 --> 00:02:13.100
to really provide
reasoning for the demands

00:02:13.100 --> 00:02:15.130
that they're making and
in some circumstances,

00:02:15.130 --> 00:02:16.160
the government doesn't even need

00:02:16.160 --> 00:02:18.250
to claim that the things are classified

00:02:18.250 --> 00:02:20.890
just that they are prohibited
from being disclosed.

00:02:20.890 --> 00:02:23.960
So who knows what they
prevented Bolton from saying?

00:02:23.960 --> 00:02:28.610
So the point of Legal Eagles
FOIA requests was to obtain,

00:02:28.610 --> 00:02:31.420
or at least force the
government to properly process

00:02:31.420 --> 00:02:33.590
these redactions under FOIA.

00:02:33.590 --> 00:02:35.790
Information that the
government was attempting

00:02:35.790 --> 00:02:39.870
to prevent John Bolton from
publishing in his book.

00:02:39.870 --> 00:02:41.900
And we also sought to obtain information

00:02:41.900 --> 00:02:44.480
about what process the
government was using.

00:02:44.480 --> 00:02:46.270
Were there any political considerations

00:02:46.270 --> 00:02:48.640
in terms of preventing John Bolton

00:02:48.640 --> 00:02:49.680
from saying certain things?

00:02:49.680 --> 00:02:51.920
And did the government prevent him

00:02:51.920 --> 00:02:53.820
from saying unclassified information

00:02:53.820 --> 00:02:55.150
that he had a right to say,

00:02:55.150 --> 00:02:57.290
because it was politically damaging.

00:02:57.290 --> 00:03:00.090
Not surprisingly, the
government has stonewalled

00:03:00.090 --> 00:03:02.090
our FOIA requests.

00:03:02.090 --> 00:03:03.920
So, we're filing suit.

00:03:03.920 --> 00:03:06.760
We are suing the government,
the White House, the CIA,

00:03:06.760 --> 00:03:07.940
the Department of Justice,

00:03:07.940 --> 00:03:09.990
the Department of Defense,
the Department of State,

00:03:09.990 --> 00:03:13.010
and a whole host of other
federal government agencies

00:03:13.010 --> 00:03:16.940
to find out what they prevented
John Bolton from saying.

00:03:16.940 --> 00:03:18.420
The goals are simple.

00:03:18.420 --> 00:03:20.840
To force the government to
disclose the information

00:03:20.840 --> 00:03:24.780
that it didn't want John Bolton
to disclose to the public.

00:03:24.780 --> 00:03:29.020
To either force them to
un-classify the information,

00:03:29.020 --> 00:03:32.180
to admit that it was never
classified in the first place

00:03:32.180 --> 00:03:35.580
and at the bare minimum
to force them to explain

00:03:35.580 --> 00:03:38.440
why and how that information is classified

00:03:38.440 --> 00:03:40.460
and why it cannot see the light of day.

00:03:40.460 --> 00:03:42.590
This is actually what
happened when Jason Leopold

00:03:42.590 --> 00:03:44.350
of Buzzfeed filed a FOIA request

00:03:44.350 --> 00:03:47.360
and eventually a lawsuit to
enforce that FOIA request

00:03:47.360 --> 00:03:49.490
for the original Mueller Report.

00:03:49.490 --> 00:03:52.150
We got a lot more information
about the vague redactions

00:03:52.150 --> 00:03:54.360
that the DOJ had actually done

00:03:54.360 --> 00:03:56.670
to the initial release
of the Mueller Report.

00:03:56.670 --> 00:03:58.810
And we found out that a
lot of those redactions

00:03:58.810 --> 00:04:00.430
were completely improper.

00:04:00.430 --> 00:04:03.420
And because I don't necessarily
trust the government

00:04:03.420 --> 00:04:06.560
to have conducted a
good faith investigation

00:04:06.560 --> 00:04:08.100
in this particular case.

00:04:08.100 --> 00:04:09.280
We also want the correspondence,

00:04:09.280 --> 00:04:11.950
to know who was making this decision,

00:04:11.950 --> 00:04:13.560
why these decisions were made.

00:04:13.560 --> 00:04:15.350
And as I covered in my other video

00:04:15.350 --> 00:04:17.450
on the whole John Bolton case,

00:04:17.450 --> 00:04:19.010
the timeline doesn't line up here.

00:04:19.010 --> 00:04:21.850
Because allegedly, one of
the government employees,

00:04:21.850 --> 00:04:25.170
cleared John Bolton's
entire book for publication

00:04:25.170 --> 00:04:28.470
only to have that decision
changed at the last minute,

00:04:28.470 --> 00:04:30.380
by a political appointee.

00:04:30.380 --> 00:04:33.340
A political appointee who
had basically zero training

00:04:33.340 --> 00:04:35.340
in terms of over-classification.

00:04:35.340 --> 00:04:38.800
It's entirely possible that
this whole process is rife

00:04:38.800 --> 00:04:41.660
with political machinations
designed to hide

00:04:41.660 --> 00:04:44.380
the white house from
unflattering information

00:04:44.380 --> 00:04:46.060
that should see the light of day.

00:04:46.060 --> 00:04:49.570
So because the government
has stonewalled our requests,

00:04:49.570 --> 00:04:50.800
we're filing suit.

00:04:50.800 --> 00:04:54.760
We're going to ask a federal
judge to enforce our demands,

00:04:54.760 --> 00:04:57.390
to make sure that the
government complies with them

00:04:57.390 --> 00:04:59.860
and to disclose this information.

00:04:59.860 --> 00:05:01.100
This is not a stunt.

00:05:01.100 --> 00:05:02.240
This is not a joke.

00:05:02.240 --> 00:05:04.970
We are actually filing a federal lawsuit

00:05:04.970 --> 00:05:09.830
to enforce our FOIA requests
as we are entitled to do.

00:05:09.830 --> 00:05:12.750
And like any good lawyer,
I have teamed up with

00:05:12.750 --> 00:05:16.240
some of the best National
Security lawyers in the country.

00:05:16.240 --> 00:05:17.440
Specifically in this case,

00:05:17.440 --> 00:05:20.170
I am working with the
National Security Counselors,

00:05:20.170 --> 00:05:22.240
which is a nonprofit organization.

00:05:22.240 --> 00:05:24.580
And their executive
director, Kel McClanahan,

00:05:24.580 --> 00:05:27.207
who has more experience with FOIA requests

00:05:27.207 --> 00:05:29.840
and FOIA litigation than
probably anyone else.

00:05:29.840 --> 00:05:32.200
And we're committed to
taking this to the mat.

00:05:32.200 --> 00:05:34.190
We want people to be actively engaged,

00:05:34.190 --> 00:05:36.750
and we want people to have the information

00:05:36.750 --> 00:05:39.340
that is important about their government.

00:05:39.340 --> 00:05:42.700
Democracy only works when
the people are informed

00:05:42.700 --> 00:05:44.250
and have access to the information

00:05:44.250 --> 00:05:45.920
that is critically important.

00:05:45.920 --> 00:05:48.240
And if the Senate isn't
going to give the president

00:05:48.240 --> 00:05:50.890
a fair trial, when it
comes to impeachment,

00:05:50.890 --> 00:05:53.130
then the only check on Executive power

00:05:53.130 --> 00:05:54.530
is at the ballot box.

00:05:54.530 --> 00:05:59.080
- The primary way that
we reign presidents in

00:05:59.080 --> 00:06:01.900
is not through impeachment,
it's through elections.

00:06:01.900 --> 00:06:03.310
- And that only works

00:06:03.310 --> 00:06:05.920
when people have the
necessary information,

00:06:05.920 --> 00:06:07.640
including the information
that the government

00:06:07.640 --> 00:06:09.950
doesn't want its citizens to have.

00:06:09.950 --> 00:06:12.410
So this will be the first
in a series of videos

00:06:12.410 --> 00:06:13.810
that chronicles the adventures

00:06:13.810 --> 00:06:16.650
of suing the federal government
to disclose information

00:06:16.650 --> 00:06:20.140
that probably should have been
disclosed in the first place.

00:06:20.140 --> 00:06:21.240
This would not be possible

00:06:21.240 --> 00:06:23.410
without the help of the
National Security Counselors.

00:06:23.410 --> 00:06:25.490
There's a link in the
description to be able to donate

00:06:25.490 --> 00:06:26.770
to the National Security Counselors,

00:06:26.770 --> 00:06:30.470
which is a 501(c)(3), so your
donation is tax deductible.

00:06:30.470 --> 00:06:32.110
And it would mean the world to us,

00:06:32.110 --> 00:06:34.510
if you would consider
donating to the cause

00:06:34.510 --> 00:06:37.540
because lawyers and
litigation are expensive

00:06:37.540 --> 00:06:39.550
and we are committed to taking this thing

00:06:39.550 --> 00:06:41.120
as far as it needs to go.

00:06:41.120 --> 00:06:44.080
Because we believe that
this cause is just,

00:06:44.080 --> 00:06:46.610
and no one else is going to do it.

00:06:46.610 --> 00:06:49.710
And any donations made above
the cost of this litigation

00:06:49.710 --> 00:06:51.480
will go towards the other charitable work

00:06:51.480 --> 00:06:52.930
that the National Security Counselors do.

00:06:52.930 --> 00:06:54.630
Which includes but isn't limited to,

00:06:54.630 --> 00:06:55.820
representing whistle-blowers,

00:06:55.820 --> 00:06:57.970
representing journalists in FOIA requests,

00:06:57.970 --> 00:07:00.680
suing to strike down
anti-transparency policies

00:07:00.680 --> 00:07:03.580
and practices and advocating
for pro-transparency

00:07:03.580 --> 00:07:06.850
and accountability reforms in
the law and the government.

00:07:06.850 --> 00:07:10.210
And it'd be great if this
was not a one time thing,

00:07:10.210 --> 00:07:12.150
I'm hopeful that this lawsuit

00:07:12.150 --> 00:07:14.590
will create real and lasting change,

00:07:14.590 --> 00:07:17.350
or at least be able to
disseminate important information

00:07:17.350 --> 00:07:19.950
related to the heart of our democracy.

00:07:19.950 --> 00:07:21.450
But it would also be great to be able

00:07:21.450 --> 00:07:23.340
to right other injustices

00:07:23.340 --> 00:07:26.770
and to be able to uphold the
rule of law in other contexts.

00:07:26.770 --> 00:07:29.640
So I'm hopeful that this
won't be a one off thing

00:07:29.640 --> 00:07:32.420
and that Legal Eagle can create some law,

00:07:32.420 --> 00:07:34.120
not just explain it.

00:07:34.120 --> 00:07:37.840
So to you Legal Eagles, I
thank you for your support.

00:07:37.840 --> 00:07:41.340
And until next time,
I'll see you in court.

00:07:41.340 --> 00:07:42.973
This time literally.

